From: Passerelle contributors <passerelle@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:51:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] docs: the x86_64 side, and what is still unverified

docs/dev/virtio-pci-notes.md states what the PCI transport assumes and how
each assumption can be turned into an observation in a guest. It is
explicit that the transport has not been run on an x86_64 QNX guest yet,
and names the two numbers that come from a boot log rather than from a
header (the MSI IRQ base and its first APIC vector), since those are the
part most likely to differ on another machine.

docs/user/qemu.md gains the x86_64 configuration (-virtfs and its long
form), docs/index.md shows both targets side by side, and
docs/dev/architecture.md stops claiming aarch64-only, records why
virtio-mmio was picked first on virt, and lists the new source files.
